  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Teko Pyahu - Rural Development Programme, Paraguay</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Paraguay Programme seeks to contribute to social inclusion and a reduction of poverty for vulnerable groups in 3 districts of the region of Caazap&#xE1; in Paraguay through a focus on building civil society capacity to advocate for more effective social policies implementation as part of the government 2020 plan. This Programme involves 3 partners, CEPAG, DECIDAMOS and CDE.

CEPAG stand for the centre of Paraguayan studies of Antonio Guash.  CEPAG seeks to contribute to achieve better social justice and equality in Paraguay and is linked to the Paraguayan Jesuits mission.  Since 1989 the Centre has been a key actor within the NGO community in implementing social research and development programmes for the poor.  

As part of this programme, CEPAG works directly with 150 members of rural organisations to provide technical assistance to farmers so that they are able to 
- Increase the quality and quantity of their produce using sustainable environmentally farming techniques, as well as to market and sell this produce to increase their family income. 
- The strengthening of their rural organizations to consolidate their internal structures to ensure they have the capacity to oversee development projects and to pressure the authorities to provide their communities with basic services.</narrative>
  </description>
